; A `match` arm's bare-identifier binder binds at the SCRUTINEE's
; type, and 555's String/Int distinction therefore holds through a
; match arm as well as through a call.
;
; `checkArms` passed a literal 0 as the expected type into
; `checkPatternTyped`, whose 0 case binds at `mkSilentWild` -
; `(mkTVar "")`, which `tyCompat` matches against everything. So a
; catch-all binder was compatible with every type at once and its arm
; body went effectively unchecked: `strLen` on an `Int`, arithmetic on
; a `String`, and a `String` returned where the signature says `Int`
; all type-checked clean. That is exactly the fiat 555 pins as
; deleted, reachable through a match instead of through a parameter.
;
; A NESTED binder was never affected - `bindPatternArgs` already binds
; each constructor argument at its declared field type - which is why
; this is about the top-level arm only, and why fixing it needed no
; change to pattern binding itself, only the type to bind at.
;
;   line 39: `strLen` on a binder over an `Int` scrutinee
;   line 44: arithmetic on a binder over a `String` scrutinee
;
; The wildcard `_` binds nothing and is unaffected, and a binder over a
; scrutinee whose type is genuinely unknown still binds at a wildcard,
; so nothing that used to check has stopped checking.
;
; `viaReturn` is here and emits NOTHING, deliberately. Its binder is
; now correctly typed `String`, and returning it from a function
; declared `-> Int` is the OTHER check - `checkDeclaredReturn`, whose
; representation comparison was Bool/Float-only until 2026-08-21 and
; names `String` since (tests/diagnostics/994 pins that check on its
; own). This case predates the closure and sat here so that closing
; the hole would show up as a change to this golden rather than as a
; silence nobody notices: line 48 now emits, as predicted.
(import Str)

(:: viaInt (-> Int Int))

(fn (viaInt n)
  (match n
    (x (strLen x))
  )
)

(:: viaString (-> String Int))

(fn (viaString s)
  (match s
    (x (+ x 1))
  )
)

(:: viaReturn (-> String Int))

(fn (viaReturn s)
  (match s
    (x x)
  )
)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) 0)
